# Security headers — continuously verified by `npm run qa:security` (qa/security/)
# and .github/workflows/security.yml. Change a header here → update the expected
# values in qa/security/run.mjs in the same commit, or CI goes red.
#
# Deliberate choices (do not "fix" without reading):
# - style-src keeps 'unsafe-inline': React style={{...}} attributes (animation
#   delays, parallax, aspect ratios) are used throughout and are governed by
#   style-src — removing it blanks large parts of the site. Revisit only via
#   style-src-attr with a full 3-engine verify.
# - frame-src was REMOVED (S25 audit fix #4): the contact map has been bundled
#   Leaflet + OSM since S16 and no Google iframe exists — frames now fall back
#   to default-src 'self'. YouTube origins were removed 2026-07-07.
# - fonts are self-hosted since S25 (public/fonts/) — fonts.googleapis.com /
#   fonts.gstatic.com are gone from style-src/font-src.
# - media-src 'self' (S26): videos were previously allowed via the default-src
#   fallback; now EXPLICIT so a future default-src edit can never silently
#   break playback. No blob:/mediastream: — all videos are static self-hosted
#   files (VideoFrame uses plain /videos/*.mp4 src, no MediaSource). The
#   qa/security video-under-CSP guard fails the build if media ever breaks.
# - img-src includes tile.openstreetmap.org: the S16 contact map's tile host
#   (images only — no script/connect surface). Update qa/security/run.mjs in
#   lockstep if this changes.
# - NO Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy on purpose — it would break the Maps iframe.
# - NO hotlink protection anywhere — it would break OG-image previews on
#   WhatsApp/social. Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin (S27) is safe
#   alongside this: CORP is enforced only by BROWSERS embedding our resources
#   cross-origin; WhatsApp/social preview crawlers fetch server-side and
#   ignore it, so OG previews keep working.
# - HSTS 'preload' is deliberately NOT set: preload is a browser-shipped,
#   hard-to-reverse commitment for the whole domain and all subdomains, and we
#   have not submitted to hstspreload.org. If that decision is ever made, use:
#   Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload
# - geolocation=(self) (S21): the contact/home "nearest branch" button calls
#   the Geolocation API on tap only; the position is used on-device to rank
#   the three branches and is never stored or transmitted.
# - script-src carries one hash (S35-FONTS): the intro-pending gate script,
#   inlined into index.html to drop a render-blocking request. A hash is a
#   targeted allowlist entry for that ONE exact script body — NOT the same as
#   'unsafe-inline', which would allow any inline script. If you edit that
#   <script> block in index.html, recompute its sha256 and update BOTH here
#   and qa/security/run.mjs's expectCsp in the same commit.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com 'sha256-IS0e94fpmBPckSIP5VCa7hb8mok6sP5VChuz/aB34E0='; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; font-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data: https://tile.openstreetmap.org; media-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com https://cloudflareinsights.com https://qzwrflxhcumnwcramrdy.supabase.co; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(self), payment=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin

# Video streaming (S27 audit fix): players must see byte-range support
# advertised before they stream — the gap read as "frozen video" on cellular.
# Live behavior differs per host (verified 2026-07-13):
# - Netlify: this rule puts `Accept-Ranges: bytes` on every /videos/
#   response, including 206s. ✓
# - Cloudflare: the EDGE does the range slicing and owns Accept-Ranges on
#   206s — it STRIPS this custom header there (CORP from /* survives, so the
#   rule engine itself works). The plain 200 carries `accept-ranges: bytes`
#   (CF adds it), and a Range probe gets a proper 206 + Content-Range, which
#   per RFC 9110 is itself the definitive range-support signal — both
#   first-touch paths advertise correctly. qa/security/run.mjs asserts
#   exactly that shape; don't "fix" it to demand Accept-Ranges on CF 206s.
# HSTS/CSP/CORP already reach these responses via the /* block above (all
# matching rules combine on both Cloudflare Pages and Netlify).
/videos/*
  Accept-Ranges: bytes
  # S38l: videos are content-addressed by NAME (a re-cut ships under a new
  # slug), never mutated in place, so they cache like the other static media.
  # Without this they fell back to the host default and were re-fetched far
  # more often than needed — costly for 2-4 MB clips on cellular.
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Hashed build assets never change — cache them hard.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Self-hosted font files (S25) — pinned upstream releases, safe to cache hard.
/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# HTML shell must always revalidate so every visitor sees the newest deploy.
/
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate

/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate

/*.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate
